    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nRecently migrating from nvim-tree to mini.files (and eventually the mini.nvim lib), I was surprised how good and lightweight it is. So thank you for this amazing library.\r\n\r\nFor mini.files, I saw some features that I felt missing compared to nvim-tree and I hope these would be considered:\r\n1. I would like to have the ability to map multiple keys for as single action like go in or go out. I usually map <CR> and <2-LeftMouse> to open directories or files.\r\n2. Is it possible to override the default behavior of MiniFiles.go_in() (opening the file in a new buffer)? In nvim-tree I was able to setup so that when opening a file it opens in a new tab (or if the file is already opened in a tab then it jumps to that tab (tab drop)).",
    "closed_at": "2024-10-27T11:40:45Z",
